6. Migrating a web application to Docker Container

Step 1: Go to https://killercoda.com/docker/scenario/container-build and login using google credentials
You may use the below 2 commands only if you face issues while running the
docker image;
[ To stop and remove the previously built image:
docker stop $(docker ps -aq)
docker rm $(docker ps -aq)

Step 2: Now Create 2 files ; app.py and Dockerfile
vi app.py
from flask import Flask
app = Flask(__name__)
@app.route('/')
def home():
    return "Hello Docker from Killercoda!"
if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=8080)

***
vi Dockerfile
FROM python:3.10-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY app.py .
RUN pip install flask
EXPOSE 8080
CMD ["python3", "app.py"]

Step 3: Build Image
docker build -t flask-webapp .

Step 4: Run the Container
docker run -d -p 8080:8080 flask-webapp

